From 2cf4f9609416fb6d87d5f1ab88105e7543a5c0cc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 07:27:07 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Tests of the regularization of Faltus et al. by kernels,
 distorted meshes

BatchIntegrationTest: cases of the regularization of Faltus et al. by
kernels compared to the integration point by point (tangent operator
assembled by kernels, applied without assembly, or assembled by MFEM with
springs; plane strain, two materials, quadratic elements, inner forces
computed element by element), on distorted meshes (new option
`distorted_mesh`: elements which are not affine and have different
shapes), also for the FBar formulation; the action of the tangent operator
applied without assembly is compared to the one of the assembled
operator; the refusal test covers both regularizations
(`testRegularizationRefusal`).

GradientsKernelsTest: the regularizations FBar and of Faltus et al. are
compared term by term to the computations element by element
(`updateResidual`, `updateJacobian`), on distorted hexahedra of orders 1
and 2, tetrahedra and distorted quadrangles, the derivatives and the
geometric data of the additional integration rules being computed; the
refusal of the regularization of Faltus et al. is removed.
